1) Application container 

--> This is the main container that runs your application.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2) Init container

--> An init container runs before the main application containers.
    It is commonly used to perform initialization tasks.
    Suppose your application requires a configuration file before starting. e.g. httpd.conf file creation , java conf file creation 
    Database initialization
    Downloading configuration
    Setting permissions
    Preparing files

--> If the init container fails: then application does not start

spec:
  initContainers:
    - name: init-config
      image: busybox
      command:
        - sh
        - -c
        - echo "configuration" > /config/app.conf

  containers:
    - name: application
      image: myapp:1.0

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3) Sidecar container

--> A sidecar container runs alongside the main application container in the same Pod.

--> They can share:
    - Network
    - Volumes
    - Pod lifecycle

--> Common sidecar uses
    - Log collection
    - Monitoring
    - Proxy
    - Security agent
    - Configuration synchronization
    - Service mesh functionality

spec:
  containers:

    - name: application
      image: myapp:1.0

    - name: logging
      image: log-collector:1.0

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

4) Ambassador container

--> An ambassador container acts as a proxy between the application and an external service.
    For example, your application needs to communicate with a database.


